    <owl:Ontology rdf:about="https://kastle-labl.org/lod/ontology/">
        <ns1:hasPatternName>Role Module Pattern</ns1:hasPatternName>
        <ns2:addressesScenario rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Use Case
                                                                Use Case Description</ns2:addressesScenario>
        <ns2:hasCompetencyQuestion rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">cq1</ns2:hasCompetencyQuestion>
        <ns2:hasCompetencyQuestion rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">cq2</ns2:hasCompetencyQuestion>
        <ns3:hasConnections rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Thing providesAgentRole AgentRole r
AgentRole hasRoleUnderName Name r st
Agent assumesAgentRole AgentRole st sd iqsf sr
Agent hasName Name r e iqsf
Name hasNameAsString xsd:string e</ns3:hasConnections>
        <ns3:hasSchemaDiagramFileName rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">M_Role.png</ns3:hasSchemaDiagramFileName>
        <dc:contributor>Cogan Shimizu</dc:contributor>
        <dc:contributor>Pascal Hitzler</dc:contributor>
        <dc:contributor>Rushrukh Rayan</dc:contributor>
        <dc:creator>Cogan Shimizu</dc:creator>
        <dc:creator>Pascal Hitzler</dc:creator>
        <dc:creator>Rushrukh Rayan</dc:creator>
        <dcterms:description rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Diagram | Intent: | An ontology design pattern for modeling Names as part of Roles, to capture scenarios where an Agent performs different Roles using different Names associated with the different Roles. Examples of an Agent performing a Role using different Names are rather ubiq- uitous, e.g., authors...</dcterms:description>
        <dcterms:title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Roledependentnames Pattern</dcterms:title>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Curated by OntoBoard 1.155.0, so that the pattern passes ODK&apos;s quality report with its default profile, names every term with a label, and is consistent and coherent. Changes: label added x20; term declared x3;
- header: dcterms:title &quot;Roledependentnames Pattern&quot; - the library&apos;s name for the pattern
- header: dcterms:description - the library&apos;s description of the pattern
- axiom removed: SubObjectPropertyOf(ObjectPropertyChain(&lt;https://kastle-labl.org/lod/ontology/hasName&gt; ObjectInverseOf(&lt;https://kastle-labl.org/lod/ontology/hasRoleUnderName&gt;)) &lt;https://kastle-labl.org/lod/ontology/assumesAgentRole&gt;) - with the chain assumesAgentRole o hasRoleUnderName -&gt; hasName it made a cycle of property chains, outside OWL 2 DL (no reasoner could answer); broken at the inverse that closes it - an agent who acts in a role still carries the role&apos;s name
- axiom removed: SubClassOf(&lt;https://kastle-labl.org/lod/ontology/Agent&gt; ObjectMaxCardinality(1 ObjectInverseOf(&lt;https://kastle-labl.org/lod/ontology/hasName&gt;) &lt;https://kastle-labl.org/lod/ontology/Name&gt;)) - the chain assumesAgentRole o hasRoleUnderName -&gt; hasName makes hasName a non-simple property, and OWL 2 DL allows no cardinality restriction on one, so no reasoner could answer; this one - on the inverse of hasName - goes, the chain stays (keeping this and dropping that chain instead leaves assumesAgentRole in two cardinality restrictions)
Each change is listed under &quot;curated&quot; in the pattern&apos;s metadata.json in OntoBoard&apos;s pattern library.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Ontology>
    


